.TH PDFLUENT-SPLIT 1  "pdfluent 1.1.0" PDFluent
.SH NAME
pdfluent\-split \- Divide a document into separate files
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpdfluent split\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-pages\fR] [\fB\-\-every\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] <\fB\-o\fR|\fB\-\-out\fR> [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR]... [\fB\-\-force\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIINPUT\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Divide a document into separate files
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Machine\-readable JSON envelope on stdout
.TP
\fB\-\-pages\fR \fI<PAGES>\fR
Pages to split out, e.g. `1\-3,5`: one file per item
.TP
\fB\-\-every\fR \fI<N>\fR
Split into chunks of N pages
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Quiet: human mode prints data only (no warnings or progress notes)
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-out\fR \fI<OUT>\fR
Output directory (created when missing)
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Verbose stderr diagnostics (repeat for more)
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Overwrite existing part files
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.TP
<\fIINPUT\fR>
Input PDF, or `\-` for stdin
.SH VERSION
v1.1.0
